@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam Style strictuml
skinparam SequenceMessageAlignment center
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam RoundCorner 10

title HCL/Lloyds PayStream: Resilient Payment Pipeline

actor "Customer / Postman" as User

box "payment-ingestor (Port 8080)" #F0F8FF
    participant "IngestorController" as API
    participant "AccountService" as AccS
    database "H2 (Local Cache)" as H2
    participant "KafkaProducer" as Prod
end box

queue "Kafka Broker (KRaft)" as Kafka #Yellow

box "payment-processor (Port 8081)" #E8F5E9
    participant "KafkaConsumer" as Cons
    participant "OutcomeService" as OutS
    database "Postgres (Persistence)" as PG
end box

== DEV SPRINT 1: VALIDATION & INGRESS ==
User -> API : POST /api/payments
note right: PaymentRequest (JSON)

API -> AccS : validate(debitId, creditId)
AccS -> H2 : Lookup Status
H2 --> AccS : ACTIVE / SUSPENDED
note over AccS, H2: Seeded from accounts.json at startup

alt If Status is SUSPENDED or NOT_FOUND
    AccS --> API : Throw ValidationException
    API --> User : **422 Unprocessable / 404 Not Found**
else If Accounts are ACTIVE
    AccS --> API : Validation Passed
    API -> Prod : dispatch(PaymentEvent)
    Prod -> Kafka : Publish Topic: 'payments.submitted'\nKey: **debitAccountId**
    note right: Keyed by debitId to ensure ordering
    Kafka --> Prod : Broker Ack (acks=all)
    API --> User : **202 Accepted** (paymentId)
end

== DEV SPRINT 2: PROCESSING & PERSISTENCE ==
Kafka -> Cons : Poll PaymentEvent
note right: Concurrency: 6 (Matches Partitions)

Cons -> OutS : process(event)
note over OutS, PG: **Transactional Boundary (@Transactional)**

group #FFEBEE [IDEMPOTENCY & RULES]
    OutS -> PG : Guard: Check if paymentId exists
    PG --> OutS : Result: New Payment

    alt Amount > £250,000
        OutS -> OutS : Set Status: **HELD**
    else
        OutS -> OutS : Set Status: **PROCESSED**
    end

    OutS -> PG : Save Outcome (Audit Trail)
    PG --> OutS : **Commit Success**
end

Cons -> Kafka : **ack.acknowledge()**
note over Kafka, Cons: **Manual Ack Strategy:** \nOffset ONLY moves after PG success.\nSurvivability during DB downtime.

footer HCL Hackathon 2025 - PayStream Architecture (Sachin - Lead Coder)
@enduml
